<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" standalone="yes"?><rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><channel><title>Machine Learning on Johnny's Blog</title><link>https://johnnyli.cc/categories/machine-learning/</link><description>Recent content in Machine Learning on Johnny's Blog</description><generator>Hugo -- gohugo.io</generator><language>en-us</language><copyright>Johnny Li</copyright><lastBuildDate>Sun, 02 May 2021 21:24:32 -0700</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://johnnyli.cc/categories/machine-learning/index.xml" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><title>Disaster Response Web App</title><link>https://johnnyli.cc/p/disaster-response-web-app/</link><pubDate>Sun, 02 May 2021 21:24:32 -0700</pubDate><guid>https://johnnyli.cc/p/disaster-response-web-app/</guid><description>&lt;img src="https://johnnyli.cc/p/disaster-response-web-app/ArpiP6q2msCtGnU.jpg" alt="Featured image of post Disaster Response Web App" /&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Disaster Response Web Application&lt;/em&gt; is a Web app that can help emergency organizations analyze incoming messages and classify the messages into specific categories (e.g. Water, Food, Hospitals, Aid-Related) during a disaster event. The app is based on Nature Language Processing and Random Forest Classifier ML model. The data was collected by Figure Eight and provided by Udacity.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The techniques I used in this project include:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;SQLite in Python&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bag of Words (BOW)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Multilabel classification&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build Machine Learning Pipeline&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Grid Search Cross Validation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Random Forest Classifier&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;K nearest neighbors (KNN)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build a Flask web app&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

 &lt;blockquote&gt;
 &lt;p&gt;You can find the full analysis in &lt;a class="link" href="https://github.com/itslijohnny/disaster-response-web-app" target="_blank" rel="noopener"
 &gt;my GitHub repo&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;

 &lt;/blockquote&gt;
&lt;h2 id="data"&gt;Data
&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;The data files associated with this project are from &lt;a class="link" href="https://www.figure-eight.com/dataset/combined-disaster-response-data/" target="_blank" rel="noopener"
 &gt;Figure Eight&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;messages.csv: FIgure Eight provide 26,248 messages&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;categories.csv: Raw categories data, total 36 categories.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2 id="project-process"&gt;Project Process
&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;ETL Pipeline&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Loads &lt;code&gt;messages&lt;/code&gt; and &lt;code&gt;categories&lt;/code&gt; dataset&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Clean data&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Feature Engineering&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Stores it in a SQLite database&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;ML Pipeline&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Loads data from the SQLite database&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;text processing and machine learning pipeline&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Trains and tunes a model using GridSearchCV&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exports the model&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Build web app&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create HTML templates&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build Flask web application&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;
